{{!--
     SHARED big-editorial-card body. (Handlebars comment, not an HTML comment:
     this partial is rendered twice, and an HTML comment would be emitted twice
     into the README.) Called with a project array as context:
       {{> project-cards _flagshipProjects}}   (featured-work.hbs — "What I build")
       {{> project-cards _clientCardProjects}} (commissioned.hbs — client work)
     Both sections must render IDENTICALLY — priority is expressed by order on
     the page, not by card size — so this markup exists exactly once. Per card:
     logo (right-float 80px) · H3 name · "For <org>" line · impact headline ·
     optional sub-project cross-links.
     The "For <org>" line iterates _affiliationOrgs (PLURAL) — eatropolis-website
     names two, Chow Luck Club Ltd and Tātaki Auckland Unlimited, because both
     reviewed the build. The list comes from organizations[].meta.x_brand
     .relatedProjectId in 60-network.yaml — NOT from projects[].clientOrgId —
     and renders in organizations[] file order, so re-ordering that file
     re-orders these logos. With a single org the output is byte-identical to
     what the old singular _affiliationOrg emitted.
     2026-07-15: the 18px tech-stack icon strip (_featuredStackResolved) was
     REMOVED from every README surface — Chan found the logo rows cluttered. The
     data (meta.x_brand.featuredStack + meta.x_brand.techIconMap) is still in the
     shards and still resolved by build.mjs into dist/profile.json; only the
     rendering is gone. Do not confuse it with _contextLogo (which harnesses a
     product supports) or _affiliationOrg (the commissioning client) — those stay.
     2026-08-12: the cross-link label is "↳ Sub-projects I built solo:", not the
     old "↳ Related:" — that read as "somebody's adjacent project" and left
     visitors unsure who built HER WAKA / GAVIGO Website / the hackathon
     assistant. Every id in relatedProjectIds is a build Chan owns end-to-end,
     and the label now says so. open-source.hbs uses the same wording.
     GOTCHA: keep the blank line between the bare <img> and the following `###`
     heading — CommonMark's type-7 HTML-block rule swallows the heading without it.
     GOTCHA: do NOT put a Handlebars comment between the impact headline and the
     sub-projects conditional below — the newline that ends the comment survives
     into the README as a stray blank line inside the card. (And never write a
     nested Handlebars comment inside THIS block: the inner close-marker ends
     the outer comment early and the rest of the file stops parsing.)
--}}
{{#each this}}{{#if logo}}<img src="{{logo}}" align="right" height="80" alt="{{name}}" title="{{name}}">

{{/if}}### [{{briefTagline name}}]({{default url repoUrl}})

{{#if _affiliationOrgs.length}}<sub>For {{#each _affiliationOrgs}}<a href="{{url}}"><picture><source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="{{default logoDark logoLight}}"><img src="{{logoLight}}" height="22" alt="{{name}}"></picture> {{name}}</a>{{#if context}} — {{context}}{{/if}}{{#unless @last}} &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{/unless}}{{/each}}.</sub>
{{else}}{{#if _contextLogo.length}}<sub>For {{#each _contextLogo}}<a href="{{url}}"><img src="{{src}}" height="22" alt="{{alt}}" style="vertical-align:middle"> {{alt}}</a>{{#unless @last}} · {{/unless}}{{/each}}.</sub>
{{else}}{{#if entity}}<sub>{{entity}}.</sub>
{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}

{{#if narrative.impactHeadline}}{{narrative.impactHeadline}}

{{else}}{{briefTagline tagline}}

{{/if}}{{#if _relatedProjects.length}}<sub>↳ Sub-projects I built solo: {{#each _relatedProjects}}<a href="{{default url repoUrl}}">{{briefTagline name}} ↗</a>{{#unless @last}} &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{/unless}}{{/each}}</sub>

{{/if}}<br clear="all">

{{/each}}
